## subscribing

i think the internet at large desperately needs to decouple itself from algorithms and recommendation feeds. to that end, if you'd like to keep up with new posts from this blog (thank you!), consider pasting the link to [`/feed.xml`](/feed.xml) into any RSS reader of your choice. it should automatically populate with previous posts, and send notications when new ones go live. you can also filter by any specific tags with `/feed/tag/{tag}.xml`, such as [`/feed/tag/commentary.xml`](/feed/tag/commentary.xml).

the full RSS feed link looks like this: `https://yareli.nekoweb.org/feed.xml`

## about the stack

this website was built myself, with HTML/CSS/JS + MD and [`11ty.js`](https://www.11ty.dev/), and hosted on [`nekoweb.org`](https://nekoweb.org).

- [**`Eleventy`**](https://www.11ty.dev/) - static site generator, blog content manager
  - [**`tailwind.css (v2)`**](https://tailwindcss.com/) - css framework and utilities package
  - [**`pagefind.js`**](https://pagefind.app/) - static search and indexing library (as seen at [/pages/archive](/pages/archive))
- [**`nekoweb.org`**](https://nekoweb.org) - webpage hosting service
- [**`Github`**](https://github.com/alittleyareli/alittleyareli) - source tracker and version control service

